Fix silent APC failures and DPD label error messages, collapse the
Couriers sub-sections (v0.128)

Dan reported three things from testing v0.126/v0.127:

1. APC's Service dropdown showed "No services available" with no error
   anywhere. Root cause: every APC response envelope carries its own
   Messages.Code/Description nested under whichever wrapper key that
   endpoint uses (ServiceAvailability/Orders/Tracks/...), and APC can
   return HTTP 200 with a non-SUCCESS code (an auth or account
   problem) - the shared send() helper only checked the HTTP status,
   so this sailed through as a "successful" empty response. Now
   checked via JsonNode.findPath("Messages") (works without knowing
   the wrapper key up front) across all three APC calls (book, label,
   service lookup) - a real problem now throws with APC's own
   description, and the Service dropdown correctly shows its cached
   fallback with a "Cached" badge instead of silently rendering empty.

2. He tested printing a DPD label in v0.126 and got "Failed to fetch
   DPD labels - DPD returned HTTP 400" with no way to tell what DPD
   actually objected to, and can't reproduce it right now to get more
   detail. Found the cause by inspection: DpdShippingService.getLabels
   discarded response.body() entirely on a non-2xx response, logging
   DPD's real reason server-side but never surfacing it in the thrown
   exception (unlike shipment booking, which already parses DPD's
   error[].message/fieldName shape via describeDpdError). Added the
   equivalent describeDpdLabelError() for the labels endpoint, so next
   time this happens the actual reason is right there in the error/bug
   report instead of requiring log access neither of us has right now.

3. Settings > Couriers wanted its three sub-sections (Collection
   Services, DPD, APC) individually collapsible rather than one long
   scroll - each is now its own nested SettingsSection, same
   collapse/expand behaviour as every top-level section on the page.

